WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.400
Procurement Intelligence Lab turns conflicting documents into reviewable, evidence-backed operational state.

00:02.400 --> 00:04.800
A procurement analyst needs a traceable answer before a requirement drives later decisions or action.

00:04.800 --> 00:07.200
The architecture preserves evidence through structured documents, assertions, reconciliation, derived facts, anomalies, predictions, decisions, actions, and human review.

00:07.200 --> 00:09.600
Gold data at every boundary tests meaning as information moves through the pipeline.

00:09.600 --> 00:12.000
Here, two eligible approved BOM revisions disagree, so deterministic policy abstains instead of inventing certainty.

00:12.000 --> 00:14.400
The processing flow retains both revisions and routes the conflict to a human with its source evidence.

00:14.400 --> 00:16.800
Procurement scenarios include quantity, missing-data, revision, price, timing, and recovery checks.

00:16.800 --> 00:19.200
Other domains are architecture candidates only; procurement is the implemented vertical.

00:19.200 --> 00:23.700
The analyst types GPU-C and the evidence cutoff character by character, then checks for discrepancies.

00:23.700 --> 00:27.600
Both conflicting BOM revisions open in context with their supporting cells highlighted.

00:27.600 --> 00:30.700
The analyst selects revision R2 and types a rationale. It governs only this item, project, and site from the server save time; the earlier unresolved assessment remains unchanged.
